-- ============================================================================
-- H3 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Process Safety: LOPA & SIL Determination, advanced
-- tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/lopa/advanced.
--
-- What this tier owns: HOW LONG THE PROOF TEST MAY RUN, AND WHAT THE ENGINE
-- DOES NOT KNOW. Sensitivity to the interval, linear and quadratic growth, the
-- longest interval and its four states; imperfect proof test coverage, the
-- floor no interval reaches below and the lifetime cap; how conservative Annex
-- B is against the time dependent route; the published example and its three
-- inferred inputs; what the engine does not do (no hardware fault tolerance
-- check, no high demand mode, no failure-rate data, credit rules that are
-- specification); and judgement end to end: a budget, a stretched interval,
-- when to redesign, the verification note. Digest sections 25 to 31, and
-- section 32.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A SIL that holds is not a requirement that
-- holds, and a target below a coverage floor is unachievable whatever the
-- interval. The Expert capstone grades three longest intervals, a PFDavg under
-- imperfect coverage, a coverage floor and a SIF stretched to a longer
-- interval.
-- ============================================================================

values ('lopa', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-proof-test-interval","title":"The Proof Test Interval","lesson_keys":["l01-pfdavg-grows-with-the-interval","l02-the-sensitivity-table","l03-linear-and-quadratic-growth","l04-the-longest-interval","l05-states-with-no-finite-answer"]},{"key":"m02-imperfect-proof-testing","title":"Imperfect Proof Testing","lesson_keys":["l01-coverage-and-the-lifetime","l02-the-floor-no-interval-reaches","l03-capped-at-the-lifetime","l04-what-a-partial-test-buys"]},{"key":"m03-how-conservative-annex-b-is","title":"How Conservative Annex B Is","lesson_keys":["l01-the-time-dependent-route","l02-where-the-forms-depart","l03-the-rare-event-warning","l04-two-out-of-two-and-common-cause"]},{"key":"m04-the-published-example-and-its-inferences","title":"The Published Example and Its Inferences","lesson_keys":["l01-reproducing-a-printed-table","l02-mrt-equal-to-the-mttr","l03-the-lifetime-inferred","l04-a-printing-slip-in-the-beta-factor"]},{"key":"m05-what-the-engine-does-not-do","title":"What the Engine Does Not Do","lesson_keys":["l01-no-hardware-fault-tolerance-check","l02-no-high-demand-mode","l03-no-failure-rate-data","l04-what-the-credit-rules-rest-on"]},{"key":"m06-judgement-end-to-end","title":"Judgement, End to End","lesson_keys":["l01-allocating-a-budget","l02-stretching-an-interval","l03-when-to-redesign","l04-writing-the-verification-note","l05-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
